    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Retry bookkeeping can abort processing of unrelated reminders",
      "description": "The new `workflowReminder.update()` inside the catch block can itself throw, escaping the per-reminder error handler and stopping the entire loop before subsequent reminders are processed.\n\nFor example, `deleteScheduledSMSReminder()` in `packages/features/ee/workflows/lib/reminders/smsReminderManager.ts` can delete a reminder while its Twilio request is in flight. When processing resumes, updating the deleted record throws; the catch block then updates that same missing record and throws again. Previously, the catch logged the error and allowed the batch to continue.\n\nMake failure bookkeeping tolerate a missing reminder (for example, using `updateMany`) and guard bookkeeping errors separately so they are logged without preventing unrelated reminders from being scheduled. Add a regression test covering deletion during an in-flight request and verifying that the next reminder is still processed.",
      "file_ref": null,
